# Local Interconnect Network (LIN) device drivers
#

config LIN_DEV_HELPERS
	tristate
	depends on LIN
	help
	  Shared driver helpers (lin-dev.ko) for host-side LIN drivers:
	  the device-side skb constructors and the owner-tagged loopback
	  synthesiser. Auto-selected by every in-tree LIN driver that
	  drives the bus from the host; users do not set this directly.
	  Modelled on can-dev.

config LIN_VLIN
	tristate "Virtual Local Interconnect Network interface (vlin)"
	depends on LIN
	select LIN_DEV_HELPERS
	help
	  Software-only LIN interface, the LIN analogue of vcan. It has no
	  hardware: the interface is its own bus. A master socket's schedule
	  drives headers, registered publishers supply responses, and every
	  resulting frame is looped back to the sockets bound to the
	  interface. Master schedule execution (unconditional, sporadic, and
	  event-triggered slots, including collision resolution), bus wakeup,
	  and the sleep command are all simulated in software.

	  Create an instance with:

	    ip link add dev vlin0 type vlin

	  This is useful for developing and testing PF_LIN applications and
	  the LIN core without LIN hardware.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called vlin.
